WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.746
People forget passwords.

00:00:02.746 --> 00:00:09.149
The Users Reset Password feature lets them recover an account by email, without asking an administrator.

00:00:09.149 --> 00:00:13.281
In this video, you turn the feature on, allow it in the settings,

00:00:13.281 --> 00:00:16.890
and follow a user from the login page to a new password.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:26.535
Without this feature, a user who forgets a password has to ask an administrator.

00:00:26.535 --> 00:00:29.115
With it, the login page offers a link.

00:00:29.115 --> 00:00:34.160
The site emails a reset link, and the link opens a form for choosing a password.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:36.942
The site needs three things.

00:00:36.942 --> 00:00:42.859
The first is the Users Reset Password feature, which depends on the Users and Email features.

00:00:42.859 --> 00:00:47.341
The second is an email provider, such as SMTP Email Provider, and the

00:00:47.341 --> 00:00:50.150
third is a setting that allows the reset.

00:00:54.369 --> 00:00:57.918
Open Tools, Features, and search for reset password.

00:00:57.918 --> 00:01:02.752
The Users Reset Password feature is in the Security category, and its row

00:01:02.752 --> 00:01:06.179
lists the features it depends on, Users and Email.

00:01:06.634 --> 00:01:07.771
Select Enable.

00:01:07.771 --> 00:01:10.840
A message confirms that the feature was enabled.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:16.012
Enabling it adds the Reset Password settings page, but visitors see nothing different

00:01:16.012 --> 00:01:17.774
until you allow it there.

00:01:19.422 --> 00:01:23.379
The reset email goes through the default email provider.

00:01:23.379 --> 00:01:30.082
Under Settings, Communication, Email, the Default provider is Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP).

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:35.641
The SMTP settings hold the Sender email address, the Host name, and the Port number.

00:01:35.641 --> 00:01:39.893
Here, they point to a local test mail server that keeps every message

00:01:39.893 --> 00:01:41.650
instead of delivering it.

00:01:45.846 --> 00:01:48.936
Open Settings, Security, Reset Password.

00:01:48.936 --> 00:01:53.236
The page has two options, and both are unchecked at first.

00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:58.274
Allow the users to reset their password turns the feature on for visitors.

00:01:58.274 --> 00:02:02.285
Until you select it, the login page shows no reset link, and the

00:02:02.285 --> 00:02:04.119
reset forms are not found.

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:05.379
Let's select it.

00:02:05.836 --> 00:02:09.907
Use site theme for password reset page makes the reset pages use the

00:02:09.907 --> 00:02:12.713
theme of the site instead of the admin theme.

00:02:12.713 --> 00:02:17.335
It requires an active site theme, so let's leave it unchecked and select Save.

00:02:17.335 --> 00:02:20.306
A message confirms that the settings were saved.

00:02:24.555 --> 00:02:27.437
A visitor who is signed out opens the login page.

00:02:27.437 --> 00:02:30.370
Because the setting is on, a Forgot your password?

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:32.623
link appears under the Log in button.

00:02:32.623 --> 00:02:33.775
Let's select it.

00:02:34.243 --> 00:02:35.725
The Forgot password?

00:02:35.725 --> 00:02:38.462
page asks for a Username or email address.

00:02:38.462 --> 00:02:42.453
Let's type the email address of Jamie Chen, a user of this site.

00:02:42.923 --> 00:02:43.946
Select Submit.

00:02:43.946 --> 00:02:47.988
The Forgot Password Confirmation page asks the user to check their email.

00:02:47.988 --> 00:02:51.416
It looks the same for an address with no account, so it never

00:02:51.416 --> 00:02:53.053
reveals who is registered.

00:02:57.306 --> 00:03:00.658
The message arrives in the inbox of the test mail server.

00:03:00.658 --> 00:03:04.436
Its subject is Reset your password, and it is addressed to Jamie.

00:03:04.898 --> 00:03:09.733
The body says whom the reset was requested for, and offers a Reset Password link.

00:03:09.733 --> 00:03:13.623
It asks the reader to ignore the message if they did not request

00:03:13.623 --> 00:03:17.068
the reset, and says that the link expires in 15 minutes.

00:03:21.268 --> 00:03:23.971
The link opens the Reset password page.

00:03:23.971 --> 00:03:27.995
It asks again for a Username or email address, then for a New

00:03:27.995 --> 00:03:30.818
password and a New password confirmation.

00:03:31.272 --> 00:03:35.912
Let's type Jamie's email address, and a password that follows the password rules

00:03:35.912 --> 00:03:38.232
of the site, in both password fields.

00:03:38.688 --> 00:03:40.245
Select Reset password.

00:03:40.245 --> 00:03:44.859
The Reset Password page confirms that the password has been reset, and offers

00:03:44.859 --> 00:03:46.748
a Click here to log in link.

00:03:47.214 --> 00:03:51.206
Let's follow that link and log in with Jamie's email address and the

00:03:51.206 --> 00:03:53.040
password chosen in the form.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.384
The login succeeds, and the home page of the site opens.

00:04:00.584 --> 00:04:03.954
A user receives at most one reset email per minute.

00:04:03.954 --> 00:04:09.098
If the email provider reports that sending failed, the user sees the confirmation

00:04:09.098 --> 00:04:14.124
page all the same, so check the email settings with Tools, Testing, Email Test.

00:04:14.874 --> 00:04:20.558
When Users Registration requires verified email addresses, users who have not verified theirs

00:04:20.558 --> 00:04:21.993
get no reset email.

00:04:21.993 --> 00:04:26.701
With the Rate Limits feature, the two forms accept 20 submissions per minute

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:28.194
from one IP address.

00:04:30.194 --> 00:04:34.632
With the Users Reset Password feature, a user recovers an account from the

00:04:34.632 --> 00:04:38.182
login page, and an administrator does not have to step in.

00:04:38.182 --> 00:04:39.624
Thanks for watching.

